/*  The Cufet parser, written in Cufet.

        cufet tools/front-end/parser.cufe <file.cufe> [more…]

    Prints each file's tree, one line per top-level statement:

        file    <the path, as given>
        (DefineStatement "total" (NumberLiteral 0) false false 1 1 _)
        …

    in the shape `ParserTreePrinter` prints the C# parser's tree — `(Kind field field …)` in each
    record's field order — so `ParserParityTests` can compare the two line for line. A file this
    parser cannot read yet prints `unsupported`, the line, the column and what it met; a file the
    C# parser would refuse prints `error` and why.

    The files beside this one hold the rest: `reader` the parser's hold on its tokens, `types`,
    `expressions`, `primaries` and `statements` the grammar, `tree` the node and its printer, and
    `scanner` the lexer they all read from.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The whole program's statements as printed lines — or the one line saying why not.
    Bind series of text or failure to program-lines, given (the text whole):
        Define found as cast tokens-of on (whole) but on failure a series of token.
        If the number of found is 0:
            Return a failure "error\tthe lexer refused this file".
        Done.
        Define reading as a new parser {
            the tokens found, the at 1, the type-depth 0, the collections-depth 0, the loop-depth 0,
            the nest-depth 0, the function-depth 0, the in-object-def false, the in-free-function false }.
        Define statements as cast listed.
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            Cast reading's skip-noise.
            If cast reading's peek-kind is "Eof", stop.
            Define next-statement as cast reading's statement or pass the failure off.
            Cast statements's add on (next-statement).
        Done.
        // The one pass the C# parser runs over the whole program before handing it on.
        Define expanded as cast expand-defaults on (statements) or pass the failure off.
        Define lines as a series of text.
        For each finished in expanded's children, repeat:
            Insert cast shown-tree on (finished) into lines.
        Done.
        Return lines.
    Done.

    For each name in the arguments, repeat:
        State "file\t{name}".
        Try to:
            Define whole as read all from the file name.
            Define lines as cast program-lines on (whole).
            For each line in lines, repeat:
                State line.
            Done.
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            State the message of the failure.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
